Algorithm 

1. Start the program.
2. Input the number of sensors and communication links, and create a weighted adjacency matrix.
3. Display a menu to apply Prim’s algorithm, update an edge weight, or exit.
4. Initialize the required arrays and select sensor 0 as the starting sensor.
5. Find the minimum-weight edge connecting a visited sensor to an unvisited sensor.
6. Select the edge, mark the sensor as visited, and display the edge weight and running total cost.
7. Repeat until no more reachable sensors remain.
8. Display the total cost and check whether a spanning tree can be formed.
9. If the user updates an existing edge weight, update the matrix and run Prim’s algorithm again.
10. Repeat the menu until Exit is selected.
11. Stop the program.
